---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "@/components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Julian, CA Vacation Rental Location Guide | 60 Min from San Diego — Salt & Sky"
  description="Our Julian, CA cabin sits at 5,440 ft near Cuyamaca Lake, 60 minutes from San Diego. Hiking, gold mines, apple pie, and dark skies — here's what's nearby."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="pt-40 md:pt-48 pb-16 md:pb-20 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
    <p class="text-muted-foreground tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-xs mb-4">Julian, California</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl mb-8 leading-tight">Historic. Untamed. 60 minutes from San Diego.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-20 md:pb-28 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Julian is a former gold rush mountain town surrounded by Cleveland National Forest, sitting at 5,440 feet elevation. It's one of the few places in Southern California with true four-season weather, genuinely dark night skies, and a pace of life that forces you to slow down the moment you get out of the car — all just 60 minutes from downtown San Diego.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The property is perched in the Julian hills with unobstructed views across the Laguna Mountains and out toward Cuyamaca Lake. It's not a rental in the sense of "a place to sleep near attractions" — it's the destination itself. Most guests spend more time on the deck than they do driving around.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed">
      That said, here's what's worth leaving the property for:
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-28 md:pb-40 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 md:gap-24">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">Explore</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-5">
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Volcan Mountain</span> — a hiking trail with panoramic views stretching to the Pacific on a clear day.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Cuyamaca Lake</span> — paddle, kayak, or fish, a short drive from the property.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">The gold mines</span> — Julian's original industry, with tours through the historic sites that built the town.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Do nothing</span> — the garden swing on the property is a legitimate itinerary item. Guests consistently mention it.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">Eat &amp; Drink</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-5">
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Mom's Pies</span> — Julian's famous apple pie, the thing most visitors come for in the first place.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Jeremy's on the Hill</span> — farm-to-table dining, a short drive from the cabin.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Julian Hard Cider</span> — local hard cider, tasting room on-site.
          </li>
          <li class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Menghini Winery</span> — natural wines with mountain views of their own.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-28 md:pb-40 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">Getting Here</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10">
      Julian is roughly a 60-minute drive from downtown San Diego via CA-79 or Sunrise Highway — no 4x4 required for the main routes (see our <a href={`${base}faq`} class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-muted-foreground transition-colors">FAQ</a> for full driving details). The elevation gain is part of the experience: you'll notice the air thin out and the temperature drop as you climb into the mountains, particularly in winter.
    </p>
    <div class="text-center">
      <a href={`${base}#booking`} class="inline-block bg-foreground text-background hover:bg-foreground/80 transition-colors px-8 py-3.5 text-sm tracking-widest uppercase">
        Reserve Your Dates
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
